  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 101 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nThe cold front will usher in a cooler, drier airmass into the region \non Saturday, leading to highs remaining in the 70s for much of the \narea (and into the low 80s for far southeast KS/southwest MO). This \nwould be well below (10-15 degrees below) the climatological normal. \nThis is supported by northwesterly flow aloft, as an upper level \nclosed High pressure system resides over the Four Corners region, \nwith an associated upper Ridge over the western CONUS. Additionally, \nSaturday will be breezy, with gusts up to 30-35mph throughout the \nday. \n\nTemperatures will gradually warm up throughout next week, with highs \nreaching the low to mid 90s by midweek. Mostly dry weather is \nexpected as we head into the beginning of August.",
